Second-gap clock-blocker bounds (codex-2026-06-03 S573)
==============================================================================
Necessary bounds for any strict sub-edge row M(S)<2/(2n-1):
  D_q: for every 2<=q<=n-1, some speed is divisible by q.
       Otherwise t=1/q scores at least 1/q >= 2/(2n-1).
  U_a: every unit antipodal shell mod C=2n-1 is hit.
       Otherwise S553's inverse clock scores exactly at the edge.
  N_j: every j/n clock is blocked by a runner at distance 0 or 1/n.
       Otherwise that n-clock scores at least 2/n > 2/(2n-1).

