Synthesis
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The expanded boxes refute the earlier floor-only reading of S572.
There are genuine audited rows in the open interval (1/n, 2/(2n-1)),
beginning with the lifted flip-set row (1,5,6,11,16,17) at n=7,
where M=5/33, and lifted/nonunit-hole rows at n=8 with M=3/23.
The sharpened bound is therefore not 'below edge implies floor'.
It is the three-gate necessary ledger: any strict sub-edge row must
simultaneously block all small denominators, all unit shells, and all
n-clock ticks.  The remaining proof target is to classify that ledger's
finite lift/nonunit families and prove they stay at or above 1/n.
